.TH IFTOP-WEB-USER 8 "October 2026" "iftop-web" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
iftop-web-user \- manage the users of the iftop web interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iftop-web-user add
.I name
.br
.B iftop-web-user passwd
.I name
.br
.B iftop-web-user del
.I name
.br
.B iftop-web-user list
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every page of the iftop web interface requires a login. There is no default
account; users are created with this command. Run it as root; it switches to
the
.B _iftop-web
user, which owns the users database.
.TP
.BI add " name"
Create a user. The password is asked for twice and must be at least 10
characters long.
.TP
.BI passwd " name"
Change a user's password. This also logs out all of that user's sessions.
.TP
.BI del " name"
Delete a user, which also ends their sessions.
.TP
.B list
List the user names.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IFTOP_WEB_CONFIG
The configuration file, by default
.IR /etc/iftop-web/config.toml .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/iftop-web/users.db
The users database (SQLite). Passwords are stored as scrypt hashes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iftop-json (8)
